      "section": "Article I’m reading —",
      "category": "article",
      "title": "How to win the Tour de France, in one image",
      "creator": null,
      "note": "([Fast Company](https://el2.fourhourmail.com/c/e5ux264rrb7hwv5o0/opfkhq/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9GYXN0Q29tcGFueQ==)).** I was led to this piece by Dr. Peter Attia ([@PeterAttiaMD](https://el2.fourhourmail.com/c/e5ux264rrb7hwv5o0/zvtghn/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9QZXRlckF0dGlhTUQ=)), and here’s a short preview: “Practically speaking, the energy savings is the equivalent of pedaling 9.3 miles per hour while actually flying down the road at 33.5 miles per hour.”",
